/// Receives up to 10 dead-letter records from the specified queue. Each
/// queue has built-in dead-letter handling: when a record has been received
/// MaxReceiveCount times without being acknowledged, it becomes a
/// dead-letter record, which usually means your queue consumer could not
/// process it. The dead-letter record stays in the same queue, and
/// ReceiveQueueRecords no longer returns it. Dead-letter records carry the
/// same data and partition key as when they were first delivered, and are
/// returned with a receipt handle. Use the receipt handle to acknowledge
/// the record with AcknowledgeDeadLetterQueueRecords , which discards it,
/// to change its visibility with UpdateDeadLetterQueueRecordsVisibility ,
/// or to restore it with RestoreDeadLetterQueueRecords , which returns it
/// to the normal receive path so that ReceiveQueueRecords can return it
/// again. Use this operation to inspect the records your queue consumer
/// could not process, so you can correct the cause and then either
/// acknowledge or restore them. A queue delivers dead-letter records while
/// it is in the ACTIVE state.
